    "q-130951": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130951",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $R$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $R$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $4$th column.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
