    "q-130962": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130962",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $Q,$ given by\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $Q$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $Q$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
