    "q-131303": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131303",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
